Quiriaci et Caesarii, item <NOTE N="1059" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> item  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4.</NOTE>  Victoris et Coronae,
Felicis et Feliciani <NOTE N="1060" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Feliciane
2. 4.</NOTE> , Cosmae et Damiani] <NOTE N="1061" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Uncis inclusa desunt</HI>  1.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0507">12.  <CITN>([7.] Cap. 59.)</CITN>  Cumque sanctus pontifex omnium
ecclesiarum suarum paternam, ut apparet <NOTE N="1062" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> ut apparet  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4.</NOTE> ,
 <COL N="0508A"></COL> sollicitudinem gereret, xenodochii Bremensis dicitur
magnam habuisse <NOTE N="1063" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Bremensis m. habuit 4.</NOTE>  curam. Quod ipse <NOTE N="1064" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> etiam
4.</NOTE>  multo
majoribus auxit reditibus quam antecessores ejus:
adeo ut praeter hospites, qui frequenter suscipiebantur,
cotidie pascerentur in hospitali pauperes
 <NOTE N="1065" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> XXIV pauperes 2. 3. in h. XXIIII paup. pasc. 4.</NOTE>  24. In quo ministerio fidelissimus extitit
Libentius, quem secum duxit ab Italia pontifex <NOTE N="1066" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> pontifex  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. Libentius pontifex, q. s. d.
a. I. 2. 3.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0508">13.  <CITN>(Cap. 60.)</CITN>  Ipso tempore magnus Otto, subjugatis
Christianaeque fidei copulatis Sclavorum gentibus,
inclytam urbem Magedburg <NOTE N="1067" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Magedbrug 1. Magdaburg 4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ita infra.</HI>  Medenburg 3.</NOTE>  super ripas
Albiae fluminis condidit, quam Sclavis metropolem
statuens, Adalbertum, summae sanctitatis virum,
ibidem consecrari fecit archiepiscopum. Is, primus
in Magedburg ordinatus, 12 annis strennue pontificatum
administravit, multosque Sclavorum populos
 <COL N="0508B"></COL> <NOTE N="1068" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> populorum 1. populo 5.</NOTE>  ille <NOTE N="1069" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> ille  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3. 4.</NOTE>  praedicando convertit. Cujus ordinatio
facta est anno imperatoris <NOTE N="(333)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0508" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0508D"></COL> Rectius dixisset Adamus  <HI REND="ITALIC">regis.</HI></NOTE>  et nostri archiepiscopi
35, et sunt anni <NOTE N="1070" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> anni  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  post ordinationem
sancti Ansgarii 137 <NOTE N="(334)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0508" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0508D"></COL> Ordinatus est Adalbertus non anno 971, ut
Adamus autumavit, sed anno 968, obiit vero post
annos tredecim, sc. 981. V. Annal. Hildeshem.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0508">14.  <CITN>([8.] Cap. 61.)</CITN>  Magedburgensi <NOTE N="1071" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4. Magadburgensi 6.</NOTE>  archiepiscopatui
 <NOTE N="1072" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> episcopatui 1.</NOTE>  subjecta est tota Sclavonia <NOTE N="1073" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Slavonia
3. 4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">saepius.</HI></NOTE>  usque <NOTE N="1074" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  2. 4.</NOTE> 
Penem fluvium. Episcopatus suffraganei quinque,
quorum Mersiburg <NOTE N="1075" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Mersburg 4.</NOTE>  et Cisia <NOTE N="1076" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Tyscia 3,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest.</HI>  Cicia 5.</NOTE>  super Salam flumen
condita, Misna vero super Albiam, Brandanburg
 <NOTE N="1077" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Brandinburgh
2. Brandenburg 3. 5.</NOTE>  et Hevelberg <NOTE N="1078" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Heuelbergh 2. Heuelbierg 3. Havelberg 4. Heuelburg 5.</NOTE>  interius vadunt. Sextus
episcopatus <NOTE N="1079" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> episcopus
3.</NOTE>  Sclavoniae <NOTE N="1080" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Sclavanie 2.</NOTE>  est Aldinburg <NOTE N="(335)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0508" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0508D"></COL> Oldenburg, urbs Wagriae.</NOTE> .
Eum, quod <NOTE N="1081" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> quem quia 4.</NOTE>  vicinior nobis est, imperator Hammaburgensi
archiepiscopatui subjecit, ibique archiepiscopus
 <NOTE N="1082" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> archiepiscopatus 6.</NOTE>  noster primum ordinavit episcopum
 <COL N="0508C"></COL> Euraccum <NOTE N="(336)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0508" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0508D"></COL> Nomen illud videtur esse Evracrus, Evracarus
( <HI REND="ITALIC">Ebrachar</HI> ), quod Evagrio melius respondet.
Legitur tamen pro eo  <HI REND="ITALIC">Everacus</HI>  Annal Sax. a. 972.
Apud Helmolum l. I, cap. 12, 13, audit ille
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Ecwardus.</HI></NOTE>  vel <NOTE N="1083" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  6. Curaccum vel 1. 3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2.
4.</NOTE>  Egwardum <NOTE N="1084" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Edwardum 2. 3. 4.</NOTE> , quem Latine
dicimus <NOTE N="1085" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Latini dicunt 3.</NOTE>  Euagrium.</P> <P COM="0508">15. Et quoniam occasio se locorum praebuit, utile
videtur exponere quae gentes trans Albiam Hammaburgensi
pertinentes sint dyocesi <NOTE N="1086" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0507" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0507"></COL> Hammaburgensis ecclesie pertinentes sint parrochie 4.</NOTE> . Haec clauditur
 <COL N="0509A"></COL> ab occidente occeano Britannico <NOTE N="1087" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Brintannico 1. Brittanico 2. Britanico 3. Britannico 4.</NOTE> , a meridie
Albia flumine <NOTE N="1088" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> fluvio 2. 3. 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  12. Sturmarios alluit <NOTE N="1130" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> affluit 5.</NOTE>  ab oriente Bilena <NOTE N="1131" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Hilena. 2.</NOTE>  fluvius, qui mergitur in Albiam fluvium <NOTE N="1132" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> flumen 4.</NOTE> , sicut
ille superior. (2. 5. 4. 6.)</NOTE> , ab oriente Pene fluvio <NOTE N="1089" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> flumine 1. 6.</NOTE> , qui
currit in mare Barbarum, ab aquilone vero Egdore <NOTE N="1090" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Egodore 5.</NOTE> 
fluvio, qui Danos dirimit a Saxonibus <NOTE N="1091" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Saxonia 3.</NOTE> . Transalbianorum
 <NOTE N="1092" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> atque  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2.</NOTE>  Saxonum populi sunt tres: primi ad
occeanum sunt <NOTE N="1093" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> sunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4.</NOTE>  Tedmarsgoi <NOTE N="1094" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Thedmarskones 2. Thiatmarsgoi
4. Thiedmarsgoi 5. Thiedmarsi 3.</NOTE> , et eorum ecclesia
mater in <NOTE N="1095" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> mater in  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4.</NOTE>  Melindorp <NOTE N="1096" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Milindorp. 3. Milindrop 2. Mildinthorp
1. Melimdorp  <HI REND="ITALIC">M.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(337)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509C"></COL> Meldorf.</NOTE> ; secundi
Holcetae <NOTE N="1097" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Holmine 1. 6. scette 2. Olcetae 3. Holsati 4. Holtzati 5.</NOTE> , dicti a silvis quas accolunt; eos Sturia
 <NOTE N="1098" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Stiriha 3.</NOTE>  flumen interluit <NOTE N="1099" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> interfluit 2. 3. 4. quorum  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE> , ecclesia Scanafeld
 <NOTE N="1100" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Scanefeld 3. Sconevelt 2. Sconenfeld 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(338)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509C"></COL> Schonefeld.</NOTE> ; tercii et <NOTE N="1101" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> qui et 4.</NOTE>  nobiliores Sturmarii
dicuntur, eo quod seditionibus ea <NOTE N="1102" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> illa
4.</NOTE>  gens frequens
 <NOTE N="1103" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> frequenter 4.</NOTE>  agitur. Inter quos metropolis Hammaburg
caput extollit, olim viris et armis potens <NOTE N="(339)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Potens armis.</HI>  Virgil. Aen. I, 531.</NOTE> , agro
et frugibus felix; nunc vero peccatorum vindictae
patens, in solitudinem redacta est. Et quamvis <NOTE N="1104" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> occulto Dei judicio vastata  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0509B"></COL> decorem urbis amiserit, vires <NOTE N="1105" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> tamen  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE>  adhuc retinet metropolis,
viduitatis suae dampna consolans in provectu
 <NOTE N="1106" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> proventu 3. profectu
2.</NOTE>  filiorum, quos per totam septentrionis
latitudinem suae <NOTE N="1107" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> sua 1.</NOTE>  legationi <NOTE N="1108" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> legatione 1. 6.</NOTE>  cotidie videt accrescere.
De quibus etiam tam laeta <NOTE N="1109" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> tam laeta etiam 2. 3. tam  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4.</NOTE>  clamare
videtur:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Annuntiavi et locuta</HI> <NOTE N="1110" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> locutus 2. 3. 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sum, multiplicati
sunt super numerum</HI>   <CITN>(Psal. XL, 6)</CITN> .</P> <P COM="0509"><COL N="0510A"></COL> 15 <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  12. Sturmarios alluit <NOTE N="1130" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> affluit 5.</NOTE>  ab oriente Bilena <NOTE N="1131" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Hilena. 2.</NOTE>  fluvius, qui mergitur in Albiam fluvium <NOTE N="1132" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> flumen 4.</NOTE> , sicut
ille superior. (2. 5. 4. 6.)</NOTE>   <CITN>([9.] Cap. 62.)</CITN>  Invenimus quoque limitem
Saxoniae quae <NOTE N="1111" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> qui 4.</NOTE>  trans Albiam est, praescriptum a
