orientali Travennae.</NOTE> ; mox in Agrimeshov <NOTE N="1123" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Crimeson 2. 5. Crimesou 3. 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(349)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0510" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0510C"></COL> Tensebeck. Conf. Helmold l. I, c. 57, 63.</NOTE> , et
recto <NOTE N="1124" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> recte
2. 3. 4.</NOTE>  ad vadum, quod <NOTE N="1125" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> qui 1. 6.</NOTE>  dicitur Agrimeswidil
 <NOTE N="1126" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Agrimeswidel 3. Agrimeswedel 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(350)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0510" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0510C"></COL> Hodie der Stocksee. V. Dankwerth Landesbeschreibung
der herzogthümer Schleswig und
Holstein.</NOTE> , ascendit. Ubi et Burwido <NOTE N="1127" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Burgwido 2. 4. Byurguido 3.</NOTE>  fecit
 <COL N="0510B"></COL> duellum contra campionem Sclavorum, interfecitque
 <NOTE N="1128" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> et
 <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  eum: et lapis in eodem loco positus est in
memoriam <NOTE N="1129" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> ubi et lapis in monumentum positus est 4.</NOTE> . Ab eadem igitur aqua sursum procurrens
terminus in stagnum Colse <NOTE N="(351)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0510" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0510C"></COL> Lacus Plunensis, cujus nominis vestigium
manet in villa Kollübbe.</NOTE>  vadit;
sicque ad orientalem campum venit Zuentifeld <NOTE N="(352)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0510" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0510C"></COL> Hodie Bornhöft, v. Helmold. l. I, c. 94.</NOTE> ,
usque in ipsum flumen Zuentinam <NOTE N="***" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  14. Zuentina <NOTE N="1138" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Llevenna 2.</NOTE>  fluvius currit a lacu, in quo Plunie <NOTE N="1139" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Plunie 2. Plinne 3. Plone 4.</NOTE>  civitas sita est. Inde per saltum vadit
Isarnho <NOTE N="1140" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> Isatuho 2.</NOTE> , mergiturque in <NOTE N="1141" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> inque 5.</NOTE>  mare Scythicum <NOTE N="1142" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0509" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0509"></COL> non longe ab oppido Kyl  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit Lindenbrogius. In cod. 3. haec ita leguntur:</HI>  Zuentina
fluvius oritur a lacu, in quos civitas Plinne sita est, et mergitur in mare Scythicum.</NOTE> . (2. 3. 4. 5. 6.)</NOTE> , per quem limes
 <COL N="0511A"></COL> Saxoniae usque in pelagus Scythicum et mare quod
vocant <NOTE N="1143" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> dicitur 4.</NOTE>  Orientale delabitur.</P> <P COM="0511">16. De cujus freti natura breviter in gestis
Karoli meminit Einhardus, cum de bello diceret
Sclavanico. <NOTE N="(353)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511C"></COL> Cap. 12.</NOTE> . «Sinus, ait, quidam ab occidentali
occeano versus orientem <NOTE N="1144" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4.</NOTE>  porrigitur,
longitudinis quidem incompertae, latitudinis vero,
quae nusquam centum milia <NOTE N="1145" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> milia  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1. c. 6.</NOTE>  passuum excedat
 <NOTE N="1146" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> excedit 1.</NOTE> , cum in multis locis contractior inveniatur.
Hunc multae circumsident nationes, Dani siquidem
 <NOTE N="1147" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> quidem 2. 3. 4.</NOTE>  ac Sueones, quos Nortmannos <NOTE N="1148" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Nordmannos 2. 3. 4.</NOTE>  vocamus, et
septentrionale litus et omnes in eo insulas <NOTE N="1149" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> insulant 1.</NOTE>  tenent.
At <NOTE N="1150" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Ad 3. 5.</NOTE>  litus australe Sclavi et aliae diversae
incolunt nationes, inter quos vel praecipui sunt, quibus
tunc a rege bellum <NOTE N="1151" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> bellum a rege 1.</NOTE>  inferebatur, Wilzi, quos ille
 <COL N="0511B"></COL> una tantum et quam per se gesserat, expeditione ita
contudit <NOTE N="1152" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> contulit 1. 2. 6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ita et codd. nonnulli Einhardi l. l.</HI></NOTE>  ac domuit, ut ulterius imperata facere
minime rennuendum <NOTE N="1153" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> renuendum
3. 4.</NOTE>  judicarent.»</P> <P COM="0511">17.  <CITN>([10.] Cap. 63.)</CITN>  Haec ille. Nos autem, quoniam
mentio Sclavorum totiens <NOTE N="1154" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> tocies 3. tocius 1.</NOTE>  incidit, non ab
re arbitramur, si de natura et gentibus Sclavaniae
historico aliquid dicemus <NOTE N="1155" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> dicamus 3. 5.</NOTE>  compendio, eo quod
Sclavi eo tempore studio nostri pontificis Adaldagi
narrantur ad Christianam religionem fere omnes
conversi <NOTE N="1156" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Adaldagi ad ch. f. sint o. r. conversi 4.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0511">18.  <CITN>(Cap. 64.)</CITN>  Sclavania igitur, amplissima Germaniae
 <COL N="0512A"></COL> provintia, a Winulis <NOTE N="(354)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511C"></COL> Winulorum nomen  <CITN>(v. infra c. 19, l. IV,
c. 13)</CITN>  aliis scriptoribus coaevis seu antiquioribus
plane incognitum. Winili vero de Scandinavia
egressi, postea Langobardi dicti, teste Paulo Diacono
 <CITN>(De rebus Langobard. l. I, c. 9)</CITN>  fuerunt inimici
Wandalorum; Helmoldus vero  <CITN>(l. I, c. 15, 19)</CITN> 
Winulos sive Winethos eos appellat. Venlas et Vinedas
bene distinxit carnem Anglosaxonicum de
poetae peregrinationibus.</NOTE>  incolitur, qui
olim dicti sunt Wandali. Decies major esse fertur
 <NOTE N="1157" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> dicitur
5</NOTE> , quam nostra Saxonia, praesertim si Boemiam et
eos qui trans Oddaram <NOTE N="1158" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Oddoram 2. 4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">saepius.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  15. Trans Oddoram <NOTE N="1177" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Odderam 3. Oderam 5.</NOTE>  fluvium primi habitant Pomerani, deinde Polani, qui a latere habent
hinc Pruzzos <NOTE N="1178" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Pruzlos 2. habent Pruxelanos 3.</NOTE> , inde Behemos <NOTE N="1179" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Boemos 4.</NOTE> , ab oriente Ruzzos <NOTE N="1180" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Ruzlos 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Verba:</HI>  inde—Ruzzos  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  3.</NOTE> . (2. 3. 4. 5. 6.)</NOTE>  sunt Polanos <NOTE N="1159" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Polanas 2.</NOTE>  qui
nec habitu, nec lingua discrepant, in partem adjeceris
Sclavaniae. Haec autem regio cum sit armis,
viris et frugibus opulentissima, firmis undique saltuum
vel terminis fluminum <NOTE N="1160" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> et fluminum terminis 2. 3. 4.</NOTE>  clauditur. Ejus latitudo
est a meridie usque <NOTE N="1161" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> usque  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2. 3. 4.</NOTE>  in boream, hoc est
ab Albia fluvio usque ad mare Scythicum. Longitudo
autem illa videtur, quae initium habet ab nostra
Hammaburgensi parrochia et porrigitur in orientem,
infinitis aucta spatiis, usque in Beguariam <NOTE N="1162" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Beuguariam 2. Benguariam 3. Bulgariam  <HI REND="ITALIC">M. F.</HI></NOTE> , Ungriam
et <NOTE N="1163" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> vel 6.</NOTE>  Graeciam. Populi Sclavorum <NOTE N="1164" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> igitur Slavorum sunt 4.</NOTE>  multi,
quorum primi sunt ab occidente confines Transalbianis
 <COL N="0512B"></COL> Waigri <NOTE N="1165" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Vagri
3.</NOTE> , eorum civitas Aldinburg <NOTE N="1166" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Aldenburg 5.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="**" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  16. Aldinborg civitas magna Sclavorum, qui Waigri dicuntur, sita est juxta mare quod Balticum
sive Barbarum dicitur, itinere die. . . ab Hammaburg. (6.)</NOTE>  maritima.
Deinde secuntur Obodriti <NOTE N="1167" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Obotriti 3.</NOTE> , qui nunc <NOTE N="1168" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> numero 2. 3. altero nomine 4.</NOTE> 
Reregi <NOTE N="1169" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Kerigi 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(355)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511C"></COL> Ita dicti Adamo, ut videtur, de emporio
eorum Reric, de quo v. Einhardi Annales ann. 808,
809.</NOTE>  vocantur, et civitas eorum Magnopolis
 <NOTE N="(356)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511C"></COL> Meklenburg, nunc villa, paulo infra Wismar.</NOTE> . Item versus non Polabingi, quorum civitas
Razispurg <NOTE N="1170" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> Razisburgh
2. Razisburg 3. 4.</NOTE> . Ultra illos sunt Lingones <NOTE N="1171" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0511" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0511"></COL> quos Lingones sunt 4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vocabulo</HI>  Lingones  <HI REND="ITALIC">in cod. 1. superscriptum est:</HI>  vel lonoges.
