9. Isaruho 2. 7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In cod.</HI>  6. Isa.nhô  <HI REND="ITALIC">litera</HI>  r  <HI REND="ITALIC">erasa.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(819)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619C"></COL> Danische Wald. Conf. schol. 14.</NOTE> , quem dicunt extendi <NOTE N="3485" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> et extenditur 4.</NOTE> 
secus mare Barbarum usque ad Sliam <NOTE N="3486" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> Scliam 9.</NOTE>  lacum
 <NOTE N="3487" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> ad stagnum
(scagum 7 <SUP>b</SUP> .) Danorum, quod Slia dicitur 7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Verba:</HI>  usque—lacum  <HI REND="ITALIC">in cod. 6. superscripta sunt.</HI></NOTE> . Ceterum flumen Egdore descendit usque in <NOTE N="3488" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> ad 9.</NOTE> 
occeanum Fresonicum, quem Romani scribunt Brittannicum.
Et <NOTE N="3489" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> At 9.</NOTE>  prima quidem pars Daniae, quae
Judlant <NOTE N="3490" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> Judland 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">semper.</HI>  Judlandia vel Jucia (Jutia 10.) 2. 9. 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">semper.</HI>  Jutlant 4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">semper.</HI></NOTE>  dicitur <NOTE N="3491" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> vocatur 9.</NOTE> , ab Egdore in boream longitudine
protenditur <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  95. Saltus Isarnho a stagno incipit Danorum, quod Slia dicitur, et pertingit usque ad civitatem
Sclavorum, quae dicitur Liubicen <NOTE N="3513" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0619" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0619"></COL> Lubicen 2.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(821)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0620" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0620C"></COL> Liubicem hic, ut supra in scholio 13, intelligendum
est de Lubeke vetere, Olden Lubeke, de
qua vide chartam regis Conradi III a. 1139, Jam. 5,
et Hemold. l. I, c. 34 sq.</NOTE> , et flumen Travennam. (2, 4, 6.)</NOTE> , habens iter tridui, si in Funem
