c. 52,  <HI REND="ITALIC">operis insignia.</HI></NOTE>  a rege
Danorum magno deinceps vir Dei honore habitus,
defuncto mox pingui Heinrico, utramque Sconiae
parrochiam, quae est in Lundona <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0627" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0627"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol. 113. Lundo</HI> na, civitas  <HI REND="ITALIC">pri</HI> ma Sconie,  <HI REND="ITALIC">tam</HI>  longe  <HI REND="ITALIC">a mari</HI>  sita est, ut a Dal <HI REND="ITALIC">bo</HI> ia. (6.)</NOTE>  vel Dalboia, recepit
gubernandam <NOTE N="3699" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0627" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0627"></COL> parrochiam, scilicet
Lundensem et Dulboiensem (Dalboensem 5.) gub. recepit 4.</NOTE> . Qui mox Lundonae <NOTE N="3700" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0627" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0627"></COL> Londone 2. 8. 9. 10. Lunde 4.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0627C"></COL> sedem suam constituit <NOTE N="3701" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0627" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0627"></COL> sedem episcopalem constituens 4.</NOTE>  apud Dalboiam vero <NOTE N="3702" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0627" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0627"></COL> vero  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest.</HI>  4. 5.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0628A"></COL> praeposituram fratrum regulariter viventium esse
praecepit. Itaque duodecim annis in sacerdotio nobiliter
exactis, clarissimus <NOTE N="3703" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0627" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0627"></COL> charissimus 10.</NOTE>  vir <NOTE N="(843)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0628" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0628D"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Clarissimus vir.</HI>  V. supra l. III, c. 62.</NOTE>  Egino regressus
a Romana urbe, mox ut domum pervenit
feliciter, migravit ad Christum. Cujus obitus et <NOTE N="**" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0627" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0627"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  114. Funensis illo in capitalibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">a</HI> b archiepiscopo  <HI REND="ITALIC">suspen</HI> sus ab of <HI REND="ITALIC">ficio,</HI>  cum sic in. . . us Romam.
. . . leret, vi <HI REND="ITALIC">ta</HI>  defun <HI REND="ITALIC">ctus</HI>  est (6.)</NOTE> 
