rex 5.</NOTE> 
fecisse <NOTE N="(923)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643C"></COL> Cap. 26.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0643">27.  <CITN>(Cap. 235.)</CITN>  Omnibus itaque <NOTE N="4126" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> itaque  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7 <SUP>c</SUP> . scilicet 5.</NOTE>  diis suis <NOTE N="4127" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> suis  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 7 <SUP>b</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE> 
attributos habent <NOTE N="4128" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> habent  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. attribuunt 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .
3. 8. 9. 10.</NOTE>  sacerdotes, qui sacrificia populi
 <NOTE N="4129" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> populis 1.</NOTE>  offerant <NOTE N="4130" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> offerunt 7.</NOTE> . Si pestis et famis imminet,
 <COL N="0644A"></COL> Thor ydolo lybatur <NOTE N="4131" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> immolant 5. 9. 10. idola immulant 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . Thor immolatur
6.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(924)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0644" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0644B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Lybare,</HI>  hoc est sacrificare, litare, ut infra
 <COL N="0644C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">libatio</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">sacrificio.</HI></NOTE> , si bellum; Wodani
 <NOTE N="4132" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> Wadani 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">et saepius</HI>  a  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  o.</NOTE> , si nuptiae celebrandae sunt, Fricconi. Solet quoque
post novem annos communis omnium Sueoniae
provintiarum sollempnitas in Ubsola <NOTE N="4133" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> in U.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. Ubsula 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">et saepius</HI>  u  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  o. Upsula 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">saepius.</HI></NOTE>  celebrari.
Ad quam videlicet sollempnitatem nulli praestatur
immunitas. Reges et populi, omnes et singuli sua
dona transmittunt ad Ubsolam, et quod omni poena
crudelius <NOTE N="4134" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> gravius 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  est, illi qui jam induerunt christianitatem,
ab illis se redimunt cerimoniis. Sacrificium
itaque tale <NOTE N="4135" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> illuc 7 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  est. Ex omni animante, quod masculinum
est, novem capita offeruntur, quorum sanguine
deos placari <NOTE N="4136" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> deos tales placari 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 3. 5. 9. sanguine tales placari 6. placacare talis
7.</NOTE>  mos est. Corpora autem suspenduntur
in lucum, qui proximus est templo. Is
enim lucus tam sacer est gentilibus <NOTE N="4137" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> gentibus 9.</NOTE> , ut singulae
arbores ejus, ex morte vel tabo <NOTE N="4138" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> tabe 7. cibo 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 3. 5. 9.</NOTE>  immolatorum
 <COL N="0644B"></COL> divinae credantur. Ibi etiam canes et equi <NOTE N="4139" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> canes, qui 5.</NOTE>  pendent
cum hominibus <NOTE N="(925)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0644" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0644C"></COL> De hominibus sacrificatis v. etiam Dudonem
l. I, init.</NOTE> , quorum corpora mixtim
suspensa narravit mihi aliquis <NOTE N="4140" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> fidelis  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  7. quidam Ch. 3. 5.</NOTE>  christianorum <NOTE N="4141" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> se  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  5.</NOTE> 
72 vidisse <NOTE N="4142" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> se vidisse 9. fuisse 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> . Ceterum neniae, quae in ejusmodi ritu
libationis <NOTE N="4143" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> ritus libatoriis 9. ritibus libatoriis 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5.</NOTE>  fieri solent, multiplices <NOTE N="4144" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> sunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI> 
5. 10.</NOTE>  et inhonestae,
ideoque <NOTE N="4145" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> ideoque ret. sunt 9.</NOTE>  melius reticendae <NOTE N="***" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  137. Novem diebus <NOTE N="4158" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> dies 7.</NOTE>  commessationes <NOTE N="4159" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> diebus
cum commessationibus 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  et ejusmodi <NOTE N="4160" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> hujusmodi 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  sacrificia celebrantur <NOTE N="4161" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> sacrificia  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7. sacrificant 10.</NOTE> : unaquaque
die offerunt hominem unum <NOTE N="4162" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> vivum 9.</NOTE>  cum ceteris animalibus <NOTE N="4163" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> animantibus 5. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> , ita ut <NOTE N="4164" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> quod 7.</NOTE>  per novem
dies 72 fiant animalia <NOTE N="4165" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> a. q. o. 7.</NOTE>  quae offeruntur. Hoc sacrificium fit circa aequinoctium
vernale <NOTE N="4166" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> Hoc—vernale  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5. 6.</NOTE> . (5. 6. 7. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> . 10.)</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(926)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0644" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0644C"></COL> Conf. Thietmar. Merseb. l. I, c. 9, I Grimm
l. I, t. I, pag. 46.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0644">28.  <CITN>(Cap. 236.)</CITN>  In eadem provintia nuper <NOTE N="4146" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0643" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0643"></COL> nuper  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0645A"></COL> contigit res memorabilis, et pro dignitate gestorum
longe divulgata; pervenit etiam ad noticiam pontificis <NOTE N="4167" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> pervenit—pontificis  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7.</NOTE> .
Quidam <NOTE N="4168" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> enim  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  5.</NOTE>  sacerdotibus, qui ad Ubsolam
demonibus astare <NOTE N="4169" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> adstare 9.</NOTE>  solebat, nequicquam <NOTE N="4170" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> nequiquam
7 <SUP>e</SUP> . ne quicquam offertorii periret juvantibus 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  juvantibus
diis factus est <NOTE N="4171" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> est ille c. 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  cecus. Cumque vir sapiens
infortunium <NOTE N="4172" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7 <SUP>c</SUP></NOTE>  orbitatis suae culturae ydolorum
imputaret, quam <NOTE N="4173" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> quae 5.</NOTE>  supersticiose <NOTE N="4174" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> supersticione 6.</NOTE>  venerans
potentissimum <NOTE N="4175" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> potissimum  <HI REND="ITALIC">M. F.</HI></NOTE>  deum christianorum offendisse
videretur, ecce ipsa nocte apparuit sibi virgo decora
nimis, interrogans <NOTE N="4176" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> interroganti 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  si in filium ejus credere
maluerit, fore <NOTE N="4177" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> maluerit
ut 9. mallet ut 10. voluerit 7 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <SUP>c</SUP> . voluit 7 <SUP>b</SUP> . vellet 5. fore  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ut visum reciperet, abjectis quae
ante colebat simulacris <NOTE N="4178" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> colebat idolis 9.</NOTE> . Tunc ille qui nichil ardui
rennueret subeundum pro hoc dono, ita se <NOTE N="4179" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> se
 <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  6.</NOTE> 
facere, letus spopondit. Ad haec <NOTE N="4180" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Haec et 10.</NOTE>  virgo: «Scito,
inquit, certissime, hunc locum, ubi nunc tantus innocentium
 <COL N="0645B"></COL> sanguis <NOTE N="4181" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> cruor 5.</NOTE>  effunditur, in meo proxime
dedicandum honore. In qua re ne tibi aliqua signa
dubietatis remaneant, in nomine Christi, qui est
filius meus, tu recipe lumen oculorum tuorum.»
Mox ille recepto lumine credidit, pertransiensque
totas <NOTE N="(928)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Totus,</HI>  id est omnis. V. supra l. III, c. 19.</NOTE>  in circuitu regiones, facile <NOTE N="4182" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> facili fide paganis 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9 10.</NOTE>  paganis
fidem persuasit, ut crederent in eum, qui se <NOTE N="4183" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> se  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  cecum
illuminavit.</P> <P COM="0645"><CITN>(Cap. 237.)</CITN>  Quibus miraculorum causis impellentibus,
statim noster metropolitanus obediens voci quae
 <NOTE N="4184" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> qui
5.</NOTE>  dicit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Respicite et levate oculos vestros, quoniam
regiones jam albae sunt ad messem</HI>   <CITN>(Joan. IV, 35)</CITN> , ordinavit
in illas partes Adalwardum juniorem, de Bremensi
choro assumptum, virum litteris et morum
probitate fulgentem. Cui <NOTE N="4185" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Qui 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  etiam per legatos clarissimi
 <COL N="0645C"></COL> <NOTE N="4186" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> charissimi 10.</NOTE>  regis Steinkel <NOTE N="4187" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Stenkil 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">saepius</HI>  Stemkil 6. Stenckil 9.</NOTE>  sedem posuit in Sictona
civitate, quae distat ab Ubsola itinere <NOTE N="4188" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> iter 9.</NOTE>  diei unius
 <NOTE N="4189" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Quibus—unius  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7.</NOTE> . Est vero iter ejusmodi <NOTE N="4190" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> hujusmodi 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE> , ut a Sconia Danorum
per mare velificans quinto die pervenias usque <NOTE N="4191" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> usque ad 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0646A"></COL> Sictonam <NOTE N="4192" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Sictonem 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  vel Bircam, juxta enim sunt <NOTE N="(929)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0646" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0646C"></COL> Conf. schol. 121.</NOTE> . Si
vero per terram eas a Sconia per Gothorum populos et
civitatem Scaranem, Telgas et Bircam <NOTE N="4193" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Rigas et Bircas 7.</NOTE> , completo
mense pervenies Sictonam <NOTE N="4194" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Sue . . . 6. Sictonam 5</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0646">29.  <CITN>(Cap. 238.)</CITN>  Adalwardus igitur magno fervore <NOTE N="4195" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> favore 9. 10.</NOTE> 
praedicandi evangelii Suediam <NOTE N="4196" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Sueoniam 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9. 10.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">semper.</HI></NOTE>  ingressus, omnes
qui in Sictona erant et in circuitu, brevi spatio
temporis ad christianam fidem perduxit. <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  138. Relatum est autem <NOTE N="4213" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE>  nobis a quibusdam stipatoribus Adalwardi episcopi, cum primum
Sictonam accessisset ad unam missarum celebrationem, ad manum oblatas <NOTE N="4214" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> oblatus 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  sibi 70 marcas
argenti <NOTE N="4215" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> recepit  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Tantae enim <NOTE N="4216" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI> 
2 <SUP>a</SUP>  9. 10.</NOTE>  devotionis sunt omnes populi arcticae <NOTE N="4217" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> aquilonaris 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . aquilonalis 8. 9. 10.</NOTE>  plagae. Tunc
etiam occasione itineris divertit Bircam, quae nunc in solitudinem redacta est, ita ut
vestigia civitatis vix appareant: quare <NOTE N="4218" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> ubi 2 <SUP>a</SUP>  9. 10.</NOTE>  nec tumulus sancti Unni archiepiscopi inveniri
potuit <NOTE N="4219" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Hoc scholion cod. 6. in codd.</HI> 
2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in textum receptum est post verba:</HI>  pervenies Sictonam.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Deest</HI>  7.</NOTE>  (2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in textu.</HI>  6. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .)</NOTE>  Conspiravit
etiam cum Sconiensi <NOTE N="4197" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Scanensi 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9.</NOTE>  episcopo, sanctissimo
 <NOTE N="4198" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> viro  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  5.</NOTE>  Eginone, ut pariter adirent illud templum,
paganorum, quod Ubsola dicitur, si forte aliquem
Christo laboris sui fructum ibi possent offerre;
omnia tormentorum genera libenter suscepturi,
ut destrueretur illa domus, quae caput est <NOTE N="4199" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> erat 5.</NOTE> 
supersticionis barbaricae. Illa enim diruta vel potius
 <COL N="0646B"></COL> cremata, fore, ut tocius <NOTE N="4200" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> tota 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9. 10.</NOTE>  gentis conversio sequeretur.
Quam confessorum Dei voluntatem piissimus
ex Steinkel <NOTE N="4201" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Steinkil 6.
Strenkil 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5.</NOTE>  in populo murmurari sentiens, callide
submovit eos a tali cepto, asserens et illos statim
morte dampnandos, et se depellendum a regno, qui
malefactores in patriam duxerit, et facile omnes ad
paganismun relapsuros <NOTE N="4202" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> delapsuros 1.</NOTE>  qui nunc credunt, sicut
in Sclavania <NOTE N="4203" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Sclavia 6.</NOTE>  nuper possit <NOTE N="4204" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> potest 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9. 10.</NOTE>  factum <NOTE N="4205" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> factum  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  9. 10.</NOTE>  vidiri.
Talibus regis allegationibus <NOTE N="4206" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> allocutionibus 5. 9. 10.</NOTE>  consentientes episcopi,
omnes Gothorum civitates peragrabant, ydola confringentes,
et multa paganorum milia deinceps lucrantes
ad christianitatem. Adalwardo postea defuncto apud
nos subrogavit archiepiscopus quendam a Rambsola
Tadiconem <NOTE N="4207" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Radiconem 6.</NOTE>  qui propter ventris amorem
domi famelicus esse <NOTE N="4208" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> fama exili esse:  <HI REND="ITALIC">conjectura Fabricii.</HI></NOTE>  maluit, quam foris apostolus <NOTE N="4209" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Verba</HI>  Adalwaldo—apostolus,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quae in textu codd. 1 et 6. leguntur desunt</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP>  9. 10;  <HI REND="ITALIC">in codd. 5 et</HI>  8 <SUP>b</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">instar scholii, sc.
nr. 95. legentur. In cod. 7. totum hoc caput, exceptis verbis sequentibus:</HI>  Haec de S.—sufficiant,  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest.</HI></NOTE> .
 <COL N="0646C"></COL> Haec de Sueonia et cerimoniis <NOTE N="4210" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> caeremoniis 9. 10.</NOTE>  ejus dicta
sufficiant <NOTE N="4211" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> sufficiunt 10.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0646">30.  <CITN>(Cap. 239.)</CITN>  Nortmannia <NOTE N="4212" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0645" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0645"></COL> Nordmannia 5. 6. 10. Normannia 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 7. 9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In cod.</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">hic
legitur inscriptio:</HI>  Incipit de Nordwegia  <HI REND="ITALIC">in 8. vero:</HI>  Incipit de regno Nordvegiae;  <HI REND="ITALIC">in cod.</HI>  9: De regno
Norwegiae;  <HI REND="ITALIC">in</HI>  10: Nordmannia.</NOTE>  sicut ultima cibis
provincia est, in ultimo libri loco convenienter
 <COL N="0647A"></COL> ponetur a nobis <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  139. Ab illis <NOTE N="4275" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> sunt 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Nordmannis qui trans Daniam habitant <NOTE N="4276" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Desepultura—Romanorum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  8 <SUP>h</SUP> .</NOTE>  venerunt isti Nordmanni, qui
Franciam incolunt, et ab his nuper Appulia suscepit tertios Nordmannos. (5. 6. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .)</NOTE> . Haec a modernis dicitur Norguegia
 <NOTE N="4220" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Nordvegia 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">semper.</HI>  Norwegia 5. 7. 9. Norwegia 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">semper.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(930)." TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647B"></COL> Nomen Nordwegae notum fuit auctori Encomii
Emmae. V. Duchesne SS. rer. Normann. p. 173.</NOTE>  De cujus situ vel magnitudine, cum prius
aliqua communiter cum Sueonia dixerimus, nunc
vero spetialiter hoc dicendum est, quod <NOTE N="4221" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> in  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  9.</NOTE>  longitudine
sua in extreman <NOTE N="4222" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> externam
2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  septentrionis plagam
extenditur haec regio, unde et dicitur. Incipit
autem ex prominentibus scopulis hujus freti, quod
Balticum appellari solet: deinde reflexo in aquilonem
dorso, postquam fremetis <NOTE N="4223" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> ferventis 5.</NOTE>  occeani marginem
suo circuit ambitu, tandem in Ripheis montibus
limitem facit, ubi et lassus deficit orbis. Nortmannia
propter asperitatem montium <NOTE N="4224" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> montium  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  9.</NOTE>  sive propter frigus
intemperatum <NOTE N="4225" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> tempestuosum 6. interpretatum 7 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  sterilissima est omnium regionum,
solis apta pecoribus. Quorum armenta ritu Arabum
longe <NOTE N="4226" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI> 
7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  in desertis stabulant. Eoque <NOTE N="4227" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> quod 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  victu peculii
 <COL N="0647B"></COL> transigunt <NOTE N="4228" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> transisigunt 6.</NOTE>  vitam, ut lacte pecudum in cibos <NOTE N="4229" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> cibis 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE> 
lana utantur in vestes <NOTE N="4230" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Quorum—vestes  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9. 10.</NOTE> . Indeque fortissimos educat
milites, qui nulla frugum luxuria molliti, sepius
impugnant alios quam ipsi molestentur ab aliquo.
Sine invidia cum proximis habitant Sueonibus,
quamvis a Danis, aeque pauperibus, non impune
temptentur <NOTE N="4231" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> tentantur 5.</NOTE>  aliquando <NOTE N="4232" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> temptentur ab aliquo 6. Sine—aliquando  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7. pauperibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  9. 10.</NOTE> . Itaque rei familiaris inopia
coacti, totum mundum circumeunt et pyraticis
raptibus amplissimam terrarum facultatem reportant
domum, penuriam <NOTE N="4233" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> provinciam 10.</NOTE>  suae regionis tali modo sustinentes <NOTE N="4234" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> sustentantes 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 7. 9. 10,</NOTE> .
Post susceptam vero <NOTE N="4235" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> autem 6.</NOTE>  christianitatem,
melioribus <NOTE N="4236" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> majoribus 7.</NOTE>  imbuti scolis, didicerunt jam pacem
et veritatem diligere, paupertate sua <NOTE N="4237" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> pauperes 7.</NOTE>  contenti
esse, immo quae habent <NOTE N="4238" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> haereditant 2 <SUP>a</SUP>  5. 9. 10.</NOTE>  collecta spargere, non
ut prius sparsa <NOTE N="4239" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> conspersa 2 <SUP>a</SUP>  5. 9. 10.</NOTE>  colligere. Cumque nefandis
 <COL N="0648A"></COL> artibus maleficiorum <NOTE N="4240" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> maleficiorum  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  9.</NOTE>  omnes ab initio servirent <NOTE N="4241" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> servierunt
7 <SUP>c</SUP></NOTE> 
nunc vero <NOTE N="4242" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> vero  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. 9. 10. n. v.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  cum apostolo simpliciter <NOTE N="4243" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  confitentur
 <NOTE N="4244" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> confitentes 7 <SUP>c</SUP></NOTE>  Christum <NOTE N="4245" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Christum  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  et hunc crucifixum. Sunt
etiam continentissimi omnium mortalium, tam in <NOTE N="4246" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> in  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7</NOTE> 
cibis quam in <NOTE N="4247" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> que  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7 <SUP>c</SUP> . molestiamque  <HI REND="ITALIC">M. F.</HI></NOTE>  moribus parcitatem modestiamque
 <NOTE N="4248" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> exercent 7.</NOTE>  summopere diligentes. Praeterea sacerdotum
et ecclesiarum tanam habent <NOTE N="4249" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> cotidie  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  9.</NOTE>  venerationem,
ut vix christianus habeatur qui non cotidie <NOTE N="4250" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> offerat
5.</NOTE>  obtulerit
 <NOTE N="4251" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> audit 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE>  ad missam quam audierit <NOTE N="4252" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> dedicationis 9. 10.</NOTE> . Verum baptismus
et confirmatio, dedicationes <NOTE N="4253" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Verum—redimuntur  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7</NOTE>  altarium et sacrorum
benedictio ordinum apud illos et Danos care omnia
redimuntur <NOTE N="4254" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> arbitramur 8.
9. 10. arbitrantur 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . arbitratur 5.</NOTE> . Quod ex avaritia sacerdotum prodisse
arbitror <NOTE N="4255" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> que  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9. 10.</NOTE>  quia barbari decimas adhuc dare aut
nesciunt aut nolunt, ideo <NOTE N="4256" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> quae gratis dari deberent 9.</NOTE>  constringuntur in caeteris
quae deberent gratis offerri <NOTE N="4257" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> et
 <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. est 7.</NOTE> . Nam et <NOTE N="4258" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> igitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9. 10</NOTE>  visitacio
 <COL N="0648B"></COL> infirmorum et, sepultura mortuorum, omnia ibi
venalia <NOTE N="**" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  140. De sepultura paganorum, quanquam non credant resurrectionem carnis, hoc tamen est
memoriale, quod more antiquorum Romanorum <NOTE N="4277" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> eorum omni  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  busta et exequias eorum omni <NOTE N="4278" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Pecuniam et arma cum defuncto (Pecuniam
cum ipso et arma ejus 9.) tumulant et si qua alia ipsi cariora in vivis fuerunt 8 <SUP>b</SUP> . 9.</NOTE> 
veneratione colunt. Ceterum pecuniam hominis tumulant cum eo, armaque et cetera quae
ipse vivens habuit cariora <NOTE N="4279" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Judaeis 5.
8 <SUP>b</SUP> . 9.</NOTE> . Quod etiam de Indis <NOTE N="4280" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> scribuntur, est scriptum 9.</NOTE>  habetur scriptum <NOTE N="4281" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Qui hoc trahunt 5. Que trahunt 9.</NOTE> . Quod
tradunt <NOTE N="4282" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> (sepeli?) ri 6.</NOTE>  ex antiquo ritu gentilium, in quorum mausoleis adhuc solent inveneri
talia, cum aut in amphoris, aut in aliis vasculis secum thesauros infodere <NOTE N="4283" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> jusserunt
9. scribuntur et de vasculis gentilium constat 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  jussissent
(5. 6. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> . 9.)</NOTE> . Apud illos <NOTE N="4259" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> tanta morum  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  1.</NOTE>  tanta morum <NOTE N="4260" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> solum 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  insignia, ut
compertum habeo, sola <NOTE N="4261" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Nordmannorum
vel Sueonum 9.</NOTE>  sacerdotum corrumpuntur
avaricia <NOTE N="(931)." TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647B"></COL> Similes Nericorum laudes legentur apud
 <COL N="0648B"></COL> Ordericum Vitalem in Histor. eccles. l. X, 767
ad a. 1098.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0648">31.  <CITN>(Cap. 240.)</CITN>  In multis Nordmaniae locis vel
Suediae <NOTE N="4262" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> nobillimi 1.</NOTE>  pastores pecudum sunt etiam nobilissimi
 <NOTE N="4263" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  6.</NOTE>  homines, ritu patriarcharum et labore manuum
viventes, Omnes vero sunt christianissimi, qui <NOTE N="4264" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Norgnegia 6.</NOTE>  in
Norvegia <NOTE N="4265" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> Quos 5 Eos enim
7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  degunt, exceptis illis, qui trans arctoam
plagam circa occeanum remoti sunt. Eos <NOTE N="4266" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> ferunt 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 6. 7. 9. 10.</NOTE>  adhuc
fertur <NOTE N="4267" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> sicut 9.</NOTE>  magicis artibus sive <NOTE N="4268" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 10.</NOTE>  incantationibus in
tantum praevalere, ut se scire fateantur, quid a
singulis in <NOTE N="4269" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> terrarum  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  5.</NOTE>  toto <NOTE N="4270" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> quae—gerantur
7 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  orbe geratur <NOTE N="4271" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> certe 10.</NOTE> . Tunc etiam
potenti murmure verborum grandia cete <NOTE N="4272" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> trahuntur 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  maris in
litora trahunt <NOTE N="4273" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> aliaque 5.</NOTE>  et alia <NOTE N="4274" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0647" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0647"></COL> istis 5.</NOTE>  multa, quae de maleficis
 <COL N="0649A"></COL> in scriptura <NOTE N="4283" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> scripturis 5.</NOTE>  leguntur, omnia <NOTE N="4284" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> omnia  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  illis ex usu
facilia sunt. In asperrimis <NOTE N="4284*" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> etiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  5.</NOTE>  quae ibi sunt, alpibus,
audivi, mulieres esse barbatas <NOTE N="4285" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> barbaros 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 7. 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">M. F.</HI></NOTE>  viros autem silvicolas
raro se praebere videndos. Qui <NOTE N="4285*" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> Hii 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  ferarum
pellibus utuntur pro vestibus, et loquentes ad
invicem frendere <NOTE N="(932)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649B"></COL> V. infra cap. 42.</NOTE>  magis quam verba proferre
dicuntur <NOTE N="4286" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> videntur 10.</NOTE> , ita ut vix a proximis intelligi queant <NOTE N="4286*" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> queat 7 <SUP>c</SUP> . intelligantur 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE> 
populis. Eadem montana Romani auctores Riphea
juga nuncupant, perpetuis horrida nivibus <NOTE N="(933)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649B"></COL> Conf. supra ad schol. 132,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Riphaeorum
montium juga.</HI>  Marcian. l. I. cap. de Euphrate.</NOTE> .
Scritefingi <NOTE N="4287" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> Scritefinni 7. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  vivere non possunt absque frigore
nivium, qui etiam feras praevolant suo cursu per
altissimas nives <NOTE N="4287*" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> Eadem—nives  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9. 10;  <HI REND="ITALIC">in</HI>  5. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">juncta sunt cum scholio</HI>  98. pervolant. . alt. rupes
8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> . In eisdem montanis agrestium ferarum
tanta est multitudo <NOTE N="4288" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> copia 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 6. 7. 9. 10.</NOTE>  ut plurima pars regionis
ex solis vivant <NOTE N="4288*" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> vivat 5. 7.</NOTE>  silvaticis <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  141. Paulus ergo <NOTE N="4324" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> ergo  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  in Historia Longobardorum <NOTE N="(942)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0650" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0650B"></COL> Paul. Diac. l. l. I, 4. qui tamen hos septem
viros dormientes esse Romanos conjecit, iisque
Scritofinos esse ait vicinos.</NOTE>  affirmat, in ultimis partibus septentrionis
inter <NOTE N="4325" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> inter  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Scritefingos in quadam spelunca oceani jacere septem viros <NOTE N="4326" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> septentrionis Scritefingos septem in q. sp. c. jacere 5. 9.</NOTE>  quasi
dormientes, de quibus est opinio diversa, et quod praedicaturi sint illis gentibus circa
finem mundi <NOTE N="4327" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> sint apud illas c. f. m. gentes 5. 9. 10.</NOTE> . (5. 6. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .) Dicunt alii ex undecim milibus virginibus <NOTE N="4328" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> Dicunt enim aliqui quasdam ex XI millibus virginum cum
sociis suis 5. Dicunt aliqui ex . . virginum 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  illud pervenisse
aliquas <NOTE N="4329" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> aliquas  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. aliquas cum sociis, quarum 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> , quarum cetus et naves monte obrutae sunt: ibique fieri miracula. Ubi
et ecclesiam construcxit Olaph <NOTE N="4330" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> Olaus 5. Olavus 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> . Olaph itaque <NOTE N="4331" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> itaque  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  rex justissimus, Nordmannos
primus Christianitati attraxit <NOTE N="4332" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> primus N. ad christianitatem pertraxit 5. traxit ad
christianitatem 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> . Magnus, filius ejus, Danos subjugavit. Haraldus <NOTE N="4333" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> Haroldus 5.</NOTE> 
frater Olaph nequissimus, Orchadas suo adduxit imperio, regnumque suum <NOTE N="4334" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0649" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0649"></COL> imperio, qui et regnum suum 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  dilatavit
