convertebantur, licet ante susceptam fidem naturali
quadam lege non adeo discordarent a <NOTE N="4429" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0653" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0653"></COL> discordabant ab 6. discordabant vera n. r. 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . a Deo discordabant
vel a. 9. 10.</NOTE>  nostra
religione <NOTE N="4430" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0653" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0653"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Uncis inclusa desunt</HI>  1.</NOTE> .] Itaque petentibus illis ordinavit <NOTE N="4431" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0653" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0653"></COL> ordinant 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
quemdam sanctissimum virum nomine <NOTE N="4432" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0653" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0653"></COL> nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. ad eorum partes  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI> 
2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 8. 9. 10.</NOTE>  Isleph.
Qui ab eadem regione missus ad pontificem,
aliquandiu retentus est apud eum cum ingenti prorsus
honore <NOTE N="(963)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0654" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0654B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum ingenti honore.</HI>  V. supra l. III, c. 16
fin.</NOTE> , discens interea quibus noviter
conversos ad Christum populos salubriter posset
informare. Per quem transmisit archiepiscopus
 <COL N="0655A"></COL> suos apices populo Islanorum et Gronlandorum <NOTE N="4440" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Grondlandorum 6. Gronlanorum 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 10. Gronlannorum 9.</NOTE> ,
venerabiliter salutans eorum ecclesias et <NOTE N="4441" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP>  5. 9. 10.</NOTE>  pollicens
eis propediem se venturum usque ad illos, ut
gaudio simul <NOTE N="4442" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> similiter
5.</NOTE>  pleno fruantur. In quibus verbis
egregia, quam habuit in legationem suam <NOTE N="4443" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> legatione sua 5.</NOTE> , voluntas
pontificis laudari potest <NOTE N="4444" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> debet 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 6. 9. 10.</NOTE> , quoniam <NOTE N="4445" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> cum 9.</NOTE>  et apostolum
discimus <NOTE N="4446" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> diximus 10.</NOTE>  ad praedicandum verbum Dei
velle <NOTE N="4447" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> male 1.</NOTE>  in Hispaniam proficisci, quod implere non
potuit <NOTE N="4448" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> De quibus noster—non potuit  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt 7, ubi scholion 151. in textu legitur.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(966)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655C"></COL> Sc. Paulus. V. Epist. ad Romanos, c. XV,
v. 24.</NOTE> . Haec de <NOTE N="4449" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> de  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1. pauca de
7.</NOTE>  Islanis <NOTE N="4450" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Island 1. 5. Ysland 7. Islandia 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9. 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">saepius.</HI></NOTE>  et de <NOTE N="4451" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 7 <SUP>c</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE> 
ultima Thyle veraciter comperi, fabulosa praeteriens.</P> <P COM="0655">36.  <CITN>(Cap. 245.)</CITN>  Sunt autem plures aliae in occeano
insulae, quarum non minima <NOTE N="4452" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> quarum nomina
7 <SUP>a</SUP> . <SUP>b</SUP> . est  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 6. 7 <SUP>c</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE>  Gronland <NOTE N="4453" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Gronlandia 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE> , profundius
in occeano sita contra montes <NOTE N="4454" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> fines 10.</NOTE>  Suediae
vel Riphea juga. Ad quam ferunt <NOTE N="4455" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> fortem 7.</NOTE>  insulam a littore
Nortmannorum vela pandi quinque aut septem
 <COL N="0655B"></COL> <NOTE N="4456" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> sex 7.</NOTE>  diebus, quemadmodum ad Island. Homines
ibi a salo cerulei; unde et regio illa nomen
accepit; qui <NOTE N="4457" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Hii 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  similem Islanis vitam agunt,
excepto quod crudeliores sunt, raptuque pyratico
remigantibus <NOTE N="4458" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> navigantibus 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 8. 9. 10.</NOTE>  infesti. Ad eos etiam sermo est
nuper <NOTE N="4459" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">redundat</HI>  1.</NOTE>  Christianitatem <NOTE N="4460" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> de christianitate 9.</NOTE>  pervolasse <NOTE N="4461" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> ad eos—pervolasse
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0655">37.  <CITN>(Cap. 246.)</CITN>  Tercia est <NOTE N="*" TYPE="Scholia" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Schol.</HI>  152. Alii dicunt <NOTE N="4500" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Judicant 5. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Halagland esse partem Nordmanniae postremam, quod <NOTE N="4501" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> que 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  sit proxima
Scritefingis <NOTE N="4502" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Scritefinnis 7. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> , asperitate montium et frigoris inaccessibilis <NOTE N="4503" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> inaccessa
7. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">In cod. 6. quaedam verba addita erant nunc rescissa praeter litteras</HI> . . . . ane. . . .</NOTE> . (5. 6. 7. 8 <SUP>b</SUP> .)</NOTE>  Halagland <NOTE N="4462" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Halangland 9.</NOTE>  insula
vicinior Nortmanniae <NOTE N="4463" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> verum  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9. 10.</NOTE> , magnitudine ceteris
 <NOTE N="4464" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> ceterisque 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  non impar <NOTE N="4465" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">In cod. 7.
hic inseritur schol.</HI>  152.</NOTE> . Haec in estate circa solsticium
per quatuordecim dies continuos solem videt
super terram, et in hieme similiter per totidem <NOTE N="4466" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> totitidem 10.</NOTE> 
dies sole caret. Stupenda res et incognita barbaris,
qui nesciunt disparem longitudinem dierum contingere
propter solis accessum et recessum <NOTE N="4467" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> recessumque 7 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE> . Nam
propter rotunditatem orbis terrarum necesse est
 <COL N="0655C"></COL> ut solis circuitus accedens alibi diem exhibeat, alibi
recedens <NOTE N="4468" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> recedens  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  noctem relinquat. Qui dum ascenderit
 <COL N="0656A"></COL> <NOTE N="4469" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> ascendit 1.</NOTE>  ad aestivale solsticium, his qui in borea
 <NOTE N="4470" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> horrea 1.</NOTE>  sunt dies prolongat noctesque adbreviat <NOTE N="4471" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> abbreviat 9. 10.</NOTE> ;
descendens autem <NOTE N="4472" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  8 <SUP>b</SUP> . 9. 10.</NOTE>  ad hiemale solsticium <NOTE N="4473" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> his qui—solsticium  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . M.
F.</HI></NOTE> ,
simili ratione facit australibus. Hoc ignorantes pagani,
terram illam vocant sanctam et beatam, quae
tale miraculum praestet <NOTE N="4474" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> praestat 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9. 10.</NOTE>  mortalibus. Itaque rex
Danorum cum multis aliis contestatus est hoc ibi <NOTE N="4475" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> sibi 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
contingere, sicut in Suedia et in <NOTE N="4476" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> in  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. 10.</NOTE>  Norvegia et in
ceteris quae ibi sunt insulis <NOTE N="4477" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Itaque rex—insulis  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0656">38.  <CITN>(Cap. 247.)</CITN>  Praeterea unam adhuc insulam <NOTE N="4478" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> regionem
1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">cui voci scriba aut corrector coaevus deletae superposuit vocem:</HI>  insulam.</NOTE> 
recitavit <NOTE N="4479" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Praeterea etiam
aiunt u. adhuc ins. 7.</NOTE>  a multis <NOTE N="4480" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> a multis  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7.</NOTE>  in eo repertam occeano,
quae dicitur Winland <NOTE N="4481" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> id est terra vini  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 8. 9. 10.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(967)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655C"></COL> De terra Winland v. Are Frodi cap. 6,
Snorro Sturleson Olal Tryggwason Saga, c. 107 seq.</NOTE> , eo quod ibi vites
sponte nascantur, vinum optimum ferentes <NOTE N="4482" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> gerentes 7.</NOTE> . Nam
et fruges ibi non seminatas habundare, non fabulosa
opinione, sed certa comperimus <NOTE N="4483" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> reperimus 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  relatione Danorum.
 <COL N="0656B"></COL> [Post quam insulam, ait <NOTE N="4484" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> ait  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. 7.</NOTE> , terra non <NOTE N="4485" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> nulla 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 9. 10.</NOTE> 
invenitur habitabilis in illo occeano, sed omnia quae
ultra sunt glacie intolerabili ac caligine immensa
plena sunt. Cujus rei Marcianus <NOTE N="4486" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Martinianus 9.</NOTE>  ita memini <NOTE N="(968)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655C"></COL> I. I., pag. 215.</NOTE> :
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Ultra Thilen</HI> <NOTE N="4487" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Thyle 5. Thylem 7.
Tylen 9. 10.</NOTE> , inquiens,  <HI REND="ITALIC">navigatione</HI> <NOTE N="4488" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> navigare 5.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">unius
diei mare concretum est.</HI>  Temptavit hoc nuper <NOTE N="4489" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> nuper  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7.</NOTE> 
experientissimus Nordmannorum princeps Haraldus
 <NOTE N="4490" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Haroldus 5. 9. 10.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(969)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655C"></COL> Haraldus Hardrade † 1066. V. supra l. III,
c. 16.</NOTE> . Qui latitudinem septentrionalis <NOTE N="4491" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> septentrionalem 7. septentrionis
2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  occeani
perscrutatus <NOTE N="4492" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> perscrutans 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  navibus, tandem caligantibus
ante ora deficientis mundi finibus, inmane <NOTE N="4493" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> inane 7 <SUP>b</SUP> . mane 7 <SUP>c</SUP> . mare 7 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
abyssi baratrum <NOTE N="(970)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Inmane baratrum.</HI>  Virgil. Aeneid. l. VIII, v.
